The instant petition under Article 226 of the Constitution of India has been filed on behalf of the petitioner seeking the following reliefs:
"(a) Issue a writ, order or declaration declaring that the entire acquisition proceedings i.e., award no. 21/92-93 dated 18.06.1992 in respect of Petitioner land/plot admeasuring 1000 sq. yards in Khasra no. 216 min and 964/218 min situated in Village Haiderpur, Delhi have lapsed in view of Section 24 (2) of "The Right To Fair Compensation And Transparency In Land Acquisition, Resettlement Act, 2013" And;
(b) Issue a writ, order or declaration limited/restricted to payment of compensation to the Petitioner as per the applicable law against the Petitioner's land/plot admeasuring 1000 sq. yards in khasra no. 216 min and 964/218 min situated in Village Haiderpur, Delhi in light of the Award no. 21/92-93 dated 18.06.1992 because the This is a digitally signed order.

The Order is downloaded from the DHC Server on 07/02/2025 at 21:31:12 Momin Raza Zaidi vs Govt. Of Nct Of Delhi & Anr on 9 January, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/64507965/
1 restoration of the land in question is not possible at this stage And;
(c) Issue a writ of mandamus directing the respondents to pay the compensation/damages against the above-said acquisition proceedings as well as against the mental pain, harassment and agony suffered by the petitioner due to the misconduct of respondent authorities."
